<idea-plugin version="2">
    <id>net.javaru.intellijIdeaPlugins.frc</id>
    <name>FRC</name>
    <version>2015.0.10</version>
    <vendor email="issues@frc-intellij-idea.java.net" url="https://frc-intellij-idea.java.net">Javaru</vendor>

    <description><![CDATA[
      <p>
      A plug-in to allow FRC development using IntelliJ IDEA rather than Eclipse. It will work with either the
      free open-sourced <em>Community Edition</em> or the licensed Ultimate Edition of IntelliJ IDEA.
      <strong>This plug-in requires IntelliJ IDEA 14.1 or later, and that you run IntelliJ IDEA via a Java 8 JRE/JDK.</strong> TODO: Add details
      </p>

      <h2>Plug-in Version Numbering</h2>
      <p>
      This plug-in is versioned via a three number version: <tt>&lt;frc-year&gt;.&lt;major&gt;.&lt;minor&gt;</tt> The first number is the
      FRC competition year.
      </p>
      <p>
      The second number indicates a major release for that year. <em>If the second number is a 0, it indicates the
      plug-in is in the beta phase for that year.</em> It will be in beta phase during the pre-season until and remain that way until
      shortly after kickoff when the new development tools are released. I will do my best to update and make available the plug-in the
      evening of kickoff or the next day. However, if there are major changes to the development tools or the Eclipse plug-in
      (from which this plug-in extracts various library and tools), it may take longer to update this plug-in. Given that I use this
      plug-in myself to support my FRC Team, I will do such as quickly as possible. I may re;lease additional beta versions while I
      polish the plug-in with new changes needed for that year. I ask for your patience in such cases ;)
      </p>
      <p>
      Finally, the third number indicates a minor release. In other words, a bug fix patch.
      </p>

      <h2>Features</h2>
      <ol>

        <li>
          <strong>Robot Project Templates</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Project templates that exactly duplicate all the robot templates included in the Eclipse release are included.</li>
            <li>Automatic downloading and configuration of the WPI Library (WPILib) is provided</li>
          </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Class Templates</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Class templates that exactly duplicate all the templates included in the Eclipse release are included as <em>File Templates</em>.</li>
            <li>Some additional class <em>File Templates</em> are included.</li>
            <li>Use IDEA's awesome <em>File Templates</em> feature to add your own <em>File Templates</em>.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>NetConsole/RioLog viewing</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>View console/logging output from the robot directly in IntelliJ IDEA</li>
            <li>You can view either in the standard Run ToolWindow or in a dedicated ToolWindow</li>
            <li>Clear the output:
              <ul>
                <li>at will</li>
                <li>automatically on a redeploy of the code</li>
                <li>automatically on a restart of the robot</li>
                <li>automatically on the logging of any configurable console/log message</li>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>WPI Library (WPILib) update checking and downloading</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Get notifications if the WPILib has been updated. No need to open Eclipse to check.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Support for Maven based projects</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Add additional dependencies more easily then you can with the default ant build.</li>
            <li>Allow for automatic running of unit tests.</li>
            <li>Allow for use of the release plug-in to cut numbered builds/releases of your code including automatic VCS tagging.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Future support for Gradle based projects</strong>
          <ul>
